## Notes
- The project already has a reasonable folder split (`models/`, `routes/`, `services/`). Phase 3 will reuse it: models stay, and controllers and config are added.
- The API has no real authentication model at all; that is out of scope. Only privileged/destructive user operations (#3) will be gated by an admin token, and the login token will become signed (#8) with the same response shape.
- Category deletion was checked for AP-10: SQLAlchemy's default one-to-many behavior nullifies `tasks.category_id`, and user deletion removes the user's tasks in a single commit. No transaction or integrity finding was raised.
- No raw SQL is used (everything goes through the ORM, and `LIKE` in search is parameterized), so no AP-02. No async code, so no AP-11. Notifications are never triggered from requests, so no AP-18.

